supralinux-desktop (0.1.0~dev7) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Move persistent SDDM defaults into the new supralinux-settings package.
  * Remove the xserver-xorg dependency that was added only for the previous
    SDDM X11 greeter path.
  * Configure the SDDM greeter for KWin Wayland instead.
  * Keep XWayland in the validated Aurora baseline so legacy X11 applications
    remain supported inside the Plasma Wayland session.
  * Do not interpret the Wayland desktop-session policy as a ban on X11
    compatibility libraries or components needed by applications/features.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <noreply@supralinux.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 01:20:00 -0300

supralinux-desktop (0.1.0~dev6) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Formalize the Aurora desktop-session policy as Wayland-only.
  * Keep xserver-xorg solely for the current SDDM greeter path; it does not
    provide or imply a Plasma X11 desktop session.
  * Keep XWayland available for legacy X11 applications inside the Plasma
    Wayland session.
  * Extend clean-rootfs and boot CI so plasma-session-x11 and its session
    launcher files are rejected from the default Aurora baseline.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <noreply@supralinux.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:42:00 -0300

supralinux-desktop (0.1.0~dev5) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add xserver-xorg for the default SDDM greeter. Ubuntu's SDDM package does
    not depend on an external X server, so a clean Aurora rootfs otherwise
    reaches graphical.target with SDDM running but cannot start its display
    server.
  * Keep Plasma user-session validation Wayland-only; this X server dependency
    supports the display-manager greeter and does not add a Plasma X11 session.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <noreply@supralinux.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:30:00 -0300

supralinux-desktop (0.1.0~dev4) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Add power-profiles-daemon so Plasma power-profile controls have a backend.
  * Add ModemManager for Plasma-NM mobile-broadband support.
  * Add rfkill and IIO sensor proxy hardware integration.
  * Add switcheroo-control as the dual-GPU D-Bus integration candidate.
  * Add Plasma's on-screen keyboard so the exposed virtual-keyboard path has a
    real backend to validate.
  * Add DrKonqi/systemd-coredump integration for KDE crash handling.
  * Add KDE SSH askpass and Qt pinentry helpers for coherent desktop credential
    prompts.
  * Keep all newly added integrations subject to clean-system and hardware tests;
    Kubuntu inclusion alone is never sufficient justification.

 -- SupraLINUX Project <noreply@supralinux.com>  Tue, 25 Aug 2026 21:18:00 -0300

